# 📄 Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Product Name

**Fairshare — Simple Budget Planner**

---

## 1. Goal & Purpose

Fairshare allows users to plan the finances of a household, including planning
recurring income and expense (budget items) both on a personal and shared level.
It then is supposed to calculate some things:

- Total household income (both per person and shared)
- Total household expenditure (both per person and shared)
- The household budget balance
- A cost split for shared expenses

Fairshare is a **planning tool**, not an accounting system. However, it allows
to track actual values for budget items and will take those into account
for statistics and forecasting.
---

## Definitions

Total household income: the sum of all income (personal and shared) for a given time period
Total household income without one-time payments: total household income excluding unplanned one-time income (planned = false)
Total household expenditure: the sum of all expenses (personal and shared) for a given time period
Total shared household expenditures: the sum of shared expenses (person_id = null) for a given time period
Household budget balance: the difference between Total household expenditure and Total household income
Net result (shared): the difference between Total household income without one-time payments and Total shared household expenditures
Shared household income total (sharedHouseholdIncomeTotal): total income from shared budget items
Shared household expenditure total (sharedHouseholdExpenditureTotal): total expenses from shared budget items (same as Total shared household expenditures)

Shared budget item: a budget item (income or expense) that is not assigned to a specific person
Personal budget item: a budget item (income or expense) that is assigned and counted toward that person
Monthly amount (of a budget item): the normalized monthly value derived from frequency rules (before sign)


Planned (budget) item: a budget item that has been planned upfront (the default)
Actual (budget) item: a budget item which has planned = false where the value differs from the planning for a specific month (also known as month override)
Category correction: a total for a category where the value differs from the planning for a specific month without tracking value for individual budget items

Personal retention value (Selbstbehalt): personal expenses kept by a person before cost split (reported as personalExpenses in costSplit)
Personal usable income: personal income minus personal retention value
Budget per person: sharedHouseholdBudgetBalanceWithoutOneTimeIncome / numberOfPersons
Personal cost share: personal income minus budget per person
Personal contribution: per-person contribution based on the cost split rules
Cost split (Kostenverteilung): the set of per-person personal contribution values and remaining budgets


## 2. Scope (MVP)

### In Scope

✔ Category management
✔ Budget item management (recurring income/expense)
✔ Person management (shared vs personal items)
✔ Monthly budget calculation
✔ Summary display:

* Total household income
* Expenses grouped by category
* Total household expenditure
* Household budget balance
* Kostenverteilung (cost split) based on shared expenses and personal budgets

### Out of Scope (for now)

✖ Multiple users/households
✖ Historical tracking
✖ Bank import
✖ Authentication
✖ Advanced forecasting
✖ Currency handling beyond a single default

### Localization Requirement

The user-facing UI must be in **German**. Code, schema, and APIs remain in English.

